§§ `The sub-paragraphs that define a term`

-- Para 40(2) and General para 2(2) borrow their meanings whole (from section 285 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 and section 82 of the Companies Act 1989).
-- the borrowed definition says the body is one
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 2(A) para 40(2) the body is a recognised investment exchange, a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD` WITH `the body is a recognised investment exchange, a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD within the meaning of section 285 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the borrowed definition says no
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 2(A) para 40(2) the body is a recognised investment exchange, a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD` WITH `the body is a recognised investment exchange, a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD within the meaning of section 285 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not known
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 2(A) para 40(2) the body is a recognised investment exchange, a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD` WITH `the body is a recognised investment exchange, a recognised clearing house or a recognised CSD within the meaning of section 285 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the borrowed definition says the body is one
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 2(E) para 2(2) the body is an overseas regulatory authority exercising regulatory functions` WITH `the body is an overseas regulatory authority exercising regulatory functions within the meaning of section 82 of the Companies Act 1989` IS JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the borrowed definition says no
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 2(E) para 2(2) the body is an overseas regulatory authority exercising regulatory functions` WITH `the body is an overseas regulatory authority exercising regulatory functions within the meaning of section 82 of the Companies Act 1989` IS JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not known
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 2(E) para 2(2) the body is an overseas regulatory authority exercising regulatory functions` WITH `the body is an overseas regulatory authority exercising regulatory functions within the meaning of section 82 of the Companies Act 1989` IS NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Para 52(3): until section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 comes into force a substituted paragraph (a) applies; once it is in force the bar has ended.
-- section 18 not yet in force: the substituted paragraph (a) applies
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 2(A) para 52(3) the substituted paragraph (a) applies` WITH `section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 has come into force` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- section 18 in force: the 'until' bar has ended
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 2(A) para 52(3) the substituted paragraph (a) applies` WITH `section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 has come into force` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Para 52(2): a lawyer is (a) an authorised person for a reserved legal activity (until section 18 of the 2007 Act is in force, a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales), (b) a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland, (c) a solicitor or advocate in Scotland, or (d) a member entitled to practise of a legal profession regulated outside the United Kingdom.
-- section 18 in force; an authorised person for a reserved legal activity (limb (a))
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 2(A) para 52(2) the person is a lawyer` WITH `section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 has come into force` IS TRUE, `the person is an authorised person in relation to an activity that constitutes a reserved legal activity (within the meaning of the Legal Services Act 2007)` IS TRUE, `the person is a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales` IS FALSE, `the person is a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland` IS FALSE, `the person is a solicitor or advocate in Scotland` IS FALSE, `the person is a member, and entitled to practise as such, of a legal profession regulated in a jurisdiction outside the United Kingdom` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- section 18 in force; only a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales: the substituted paragraph no longer applies
#ASSERT (`sch 2 part 2(A) para 52(2) the person is a lawyer` WITH `section 18 of the Legal Services Act 2007 has come into force` IS TRUE, `the person is an authorised person in relation to an activity that constitutes a reserved legal activity (within the meaning of the Legal Services Act 2007)` IS FALSE, `the person is a solicitor or barrister in England and Wales` IS TRUE, `the person is a solicitor or barrister in Northern Ireland` IS FALSE, `the person is a solicitor or advocate in Scotland` IS FALSE, `the person is a member, and entitled to practise as such, of a legal profession regulated in a jurisdiction outside the United Kingdom` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
